1
00:00:00,613 --> 00:00:03,403
(Howard:)Yes, you're delicious caramel too.

2
00:00:08,496 --> 00:00:10,246
(Penny:)I will tell you why it's wrong--

3
00:00:10,415 --> 00:00:12,835
(Sheldon:)-Excuse me, may I interject?
-What?

4
00:00:13,001 --> 00:00:16,091
(Sheldon:)Biologically speaking,
Howard is perfectly justified...

5
00:00:16,254 --> 00:00:20,424
(Sheldon:)...in seeking out the optimum mate
for the propagation of his genetic line.

6
00:00:20,633 --> 00:00:21,673
(Howard:)Thank you, Sheldon.

7
00:00:21,843 --> 00:00:24,593
(Sheldon:)Whether that propagation
is in the interest of humanity...

8
00:00:24,762 --> 00:00:27,012
...is an entirely different question.

9
00:00:29,142 --> 00:00:34,022
IRA [OVER RADIO]: This is Ira Flatow and
you're listening to NPR's Science Friday.

10
00:00:34,189 --> 00:00:36,859
(Radio:)Joining us today by phone
from his office in Pasadena, California...

11
00:00:37,025 --> 00:00:38,065
[AIR HISSING]

12
00:00:38,234 --> 00:00:39,904
(Radio:)...is Dr. Sheldon Cooper.

13
00:00:40,069 --> 00:00:42,659
Oh, this is gonna be a riot.

14
00:00:42,822 --> 00:00:44,862
[AIR HISSING]

15
00:00:45,241 --> 00:00:47,621
(Radio:)Thanks for being with us today,
Dr. Cooper.

16
00:00:47,785 --> 00:00:49,415
(Sheldon:)My pleasure, Ira.

17
00:00:49,579 --> 00:00:52,619
(Ira:)Now, let's talk
about magnetic monopoles.

18
